hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2670","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bishr, narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Ibn Jurayj, who informed me Ata ibn Abi Rabah, narrated to me Safwan ibn Ya'la ibn Umayya, that Ya'la ibn Umayya said to Umar ibn al-Khattab (RA): \I wish I could see the Prophet (ﷺ) at the time when revelation is being revealed to him.\"" Then when the Prophet (ﷺ) was at Ji'rana"," he had a garment with a canopy draped over it"," and a group of his companions were with him. A man came to him who had applied perfume to himself"," and he said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what is your ruling on a man who entered the state of ihram wearing a jubbah (a long"," buttoned cloak) after applying perfume?\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) looked at him for a short while"," then revelation was sent down upon him. Umar (RA) sent for Ya'la to come to him"," so Ya'la came and put his head into the area where the Prophet was seated"," and he saw that the Prophet's face was flushed red"," just as it was during that moment of revelation"," then the revelation subsided. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Where is the man who asked me about the Umrah a short while ago?\"" The man was sought out and brought forward"," and the Prophet (ﷺ) gave a command regarding him"," saying: \""As for the perfume you have applied to yourself"," wash it off three times"," and as for the jubbah you are wearing"," remove it"," then perform your Umrah just as you perform your Hajj.\"" [Sahih]"""
